{"step_index":57,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-07T07:40:57Z","input_tokens":433,"cache_read_tokens":106292,"output_tokens":7768,"content":"While the scaffold finishes, I'll write the Bibi AI guardrails module (pure functions, no dependencies).","thinking":"I'm building a pure guardrails module for Bibi that masks personal info like emails, phone numbers, addresses, RT/RW, school names, and full names mentioned in text.\n\nBeyond masking, I'm adding injection detection that catches prompt manipulation attempts (like \"abaikan instruksi\" or \"ignore previous instructions\") and separates those from kids directly asking for answers—injections get a canned redirect, while answer-requests still reach the model with a gentle refusal hint. I'm also sketching out a small Indonesian/English profanity list for unsafe content detection, though I'm being careful about words like \"anjing\" that could mean either a curse or just \"dog\" in an innocent context.\n\nFor sensitive topics like self-harm, I want a caring safety response pointing kids toward trusted adults rather than ignoring it. I'm also planning an output filter that strips URLs/PII and checks for solution leaks by comparing output sentences against a flattened list of the mission's expected action labels.\n\nI need to be careful though, since the PRD's own example (\"siram, ulangi 5 kali\") looks like it would trigger a naive leak check, so I'm reconsidering the threshold — maybe only flag a leak when the full ordered sequence of three or more distinct action labels appears together, rather than any partial match.\n\nFor L3-M1 I should normalize labels loosely—accepting variant phrasing like \"kalau\" for \"jika\" and stripping prefixes like \"ke \" from action labels—and build the signature from just the core condition and action text, dropping connector words like \"lainnya\".\n\nSo that phrasing without \"jika\"/\"lainnya\" is safe. For the maju×3 mission, I need to detect leaks when tokens like \"maju\" repeat three times in sequence, while also considering shorthand like \"maju 3x\" or \"maju sebanyak 3 kali\" as equivalent leaks, which complicates the matching logic a bit but is reasonable to handle with a flexible check.\n\nBuilding the repeat-detection regex...\n\nNow I'm thinking about the leak threshold — how many solution blocks need to appear in a hint before it counts as giving away too much. For small solutions like L2-M1's two-block repeat structure, I need a lower bar since even a minimal hint might spell out the whole answer, so I'm leaning toward requiring at least two matching tokens in order before flagging it as a leak, while checking how single-token solutions like L1-M1's compressed \"maju 3\" would behave under that rule.\n\nI also need to normalize label text (lowercase, strip curly quotes, escape regex special characters like \"+\") before matching, and strip prefixes like \"ke\" from location labels. Then I'm sketching out the tier-decision and hint-selection functions that pick an authored hint based on session history and failed attempts, with tier-3 hints possibly blending in diagnosis-specific phrasing.\n\nFor quick questions like \"I'm confused where to start\" or \"explain with an example,\" I'm mapping each to a forced or minimum hint tier. Next I need to set up the Gemini call module, though I should verify the actual API surface after installing the package.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import type { Block, Mission, Palette } from \"@/lib/engine/types\";\n\n/**\n * Server-side guardrails for \"Tanya Bibi AI\" (FR-AI-S1..S4).\n * These are deliberately conservative: when in doubt, Bibi redirects gently\n * back to the mission instead of answering.\n */\n\nexport const MAX_INPUT_CHARS = 280;\n\nexport const FALLBACK_MESSAGE = \"Bibi lagi istirahat sebentar, coba lagi ya! ☕\";\nexport const INJECTION_REPLY =\n  \"Hihi, Bibi tetap Bibi, ya! 😊 Bibi di sini untuk menemanimu menyelesaikan misi. Yuk, lihat lagi blok-blokmu!\";\nexport const UNSAFE_REPLY =\n  \"Yuk, kita pakai kata-kata yang baik ya. 🌈 Bibi siap bantu misimu kalau kamu mau!\";\nexport const WELLBEING_REPLY =\n  \"Bibi dengar kamu sedang merasa tidak nyaman. 💛 Ceritakan ke orang tua, guru, atau orang dewasa yang kamu percaya, ya. Mereka sayang kamu.\";\nexport const LEAK_REPLY =\n  \"Ups, Bibi hampir membocorkan jawabannya! 🙊 Coba pikirkan lagi langkah pertama, kamu pasti bisa.\";\nexport const OFFTOPIC_REPLY =\n  \"Pertanyaan yang seru! Tapi sekarang kita fokus ke misi dulu, ya. 🚀 Mau Bibi bantu bagian mana?\";\n\n/* -------------------------------- Normalize -------------------------------- */\n\nexport function normalize(text: string): string {\n  return text\n    .toLowerCase()\n    .normalize(\"NFKC\")\n    .replace(/[\\u2018\\u2019\\u201C\\u201D]/g, '\"')\n    .replace(/\\s+/g, \" \")\n    .trim();\n}\n\n/* ----------------------------------- PII ----------------------------------- */\n\nconst PII_PATTERNS: { re: RegExp; label: string }[] = [\n  { re: /[\\w.+-]+@[\\w-]+\\.[\\w.-]+/gi, label: \"[email disamarkan]\" },\n  { re: /(?:\\+62|62|0)8\\d[\\d\\s-]{6,12}\\d/g, label: \"[nomor disamarkan]\" },\n  { re: /\\b\\d{9,}\\b/g, label: \"[nomor disamarkan]\" },\n  {\n    re: /\\b(?:jalan|jln\\.?|jl\\.?|gang|gg\\.?|komplek|perumahan|perum\\.?)\\s+[\\w.'-]+(?:\\s+(?:no\\.?|nomor)?\\s*[\\w./-]+){0,4}/gi,\n    label: \"[alamat disamarkan]\",\n  },\n  { re: /\\brt\\s*\\.?\\s*\\d+\\s*\\/?\\s*rw\\s*\\.?\\s*\\d+/gi, label: \"[alamat disamarkan]\" },\n  {\n    re: /\\b(?:sd|sdn|sdit|mi|min|sekolah dasar)\\s+(?:negeri\\s+|swasta\\s+|islam\\s+|kristen\\s+|katolik\\s+)?[\\w.'-]+(?:\\s+[\\w.'-]+){0,2}/gi,\n    label: \"[sekolah disamarkan]\",\n  },\n  {\n    re: /\\b(nama(?:ku| aku| saya)?(?: adalah)?|aku bernama|saya bernama)\\s+[a-z][\\w'-]*(?:\\s+[a-z][\\w'-]*){1,3}/gi,\n    label: \"$1 [nama disamarkan]\",\n  },\n  { re: /https?:\\/\\/\\S+|www\\.\\S+/gi, label: \"[tautan disamarkan]\" },\n];\n\n/** FR-AI-S4: mask personal data before it is sent to the model or stored. */\nexport function maskPII(text: string): { text: string; masked: boolean } {\n  let out = text;\n  for (const { re, label } of PII_PATTERNS) out = out.replace(re, label);\n  return { text: out, masked: out !== text };\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------ Classification ----------------------------- */\n\nconst INJECTION_PATTERNS = [\n  /abaikan\\s+(semua\\s+|seluruh\\s+)?(instruksi|perintah|aturan|arahan)/,\n  /lupakan\\s+(semua\\s+)?(instruksi|perintah|aturan)/,\n  /ignore\\s+(all\\s+|any\\s+|the\\s+)?(previous|prior|above)?\\s*(instructions|rules|prompts?)/,\n  /system\\s*prompt|prompt\\s*sistem|instruksi\\s*sistem/,\n  /(kamu|anda)\\s+(sekarang|mulai sekarang)\\s+(adalah|jadi|menjadi)/,\n  /pura[- ]?pura\\s+(jadi|menjadi)/,\n  /\\b(jailbreak|dan mode|developer mode|mode pengembang|roleplay)\\b/,\n  /you\\s+are\\s+now|act\\s+as|pretend\\s+to\\s+be/,\n];\n\nconst ANSWER_REQUEST_PATTERNS = [\n  /(kasih|beri|berikan|kasi|tunjukkan|sebutkan|tulis(kan)?)\\s+(aku\\s+|saya\\s+)?(jawaban|solusi|kunci|susunan|urutan blok|program)(nya)?/,\n  /(jawaban|solusi|kunci jawaban)(nya)?\\s+(apa|dong|lengkap|langsung)/,\n  /apa\\s+(jawaban|solusi)(nya)?/,\n  /(susunan|urutan)\\s+blok(nya)?\\s+(yang\\s+)?(benar|lengkap)/,\n  /(kerjakan|selesaikan)\\s+(misi|soal)(nya)?\\s+(untuk|buat)\\s*(ku|aku|saya)/,\n];\n\nconst PROFANITY = [\n  \"bangsat\", \"bajingan\", \"goblok\", \"tolol\", \"kontol\", \"memek\", \"ngentot\", \"kampret\", \"brengsek\",\n  \"tai\", \"setan lu\", \"babi lu\", \"fuck\", \"shit\", \"bitch\", \"asshole\", \"dick\",\n];\nconst ADULT_TOPICS = [\n  \"porno\", \"porn\", \"seks\", \"sex\", \"bugil\", \"telanjang\", \"narkoba\", \"ganja\", \"sabu\", \"judi\", \"slot online\",\n  \"rokok\", \"vape\", \"miras\", \"mabuk\", \"senjata api\", \"pistol\", \"bom\", \"pacaran\",\n];\nconst WELLBEING = [\n  \"bunuh diri\", \"ingin mati\", \"pengen mati\", \"mau mati\", \"menyakiti diri\", \"dipukul\", \"dibully\", \"di-bully\",\n  \"dirundung\", \"disakiti\",\n];\n\nfunction containsWord(text: string, words: string[]): boolean {\n  return words.some((w) => new RegExp(`(^|[^a-z])${w.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, \"\\\\$&\")}($|[^a-z])`).test(text));\n}\n\nexport type InputVerdict =\n  | { kind: \"ok\"; answerRequest: boolean }\n  | { kind: \"injection\" }\n  | { kind: \"unsafe\" }\n  | { kind: \"wellbeing\" }\n  | { kind: \"empty\" };\n\n/** FR-AI-S2 / S3: server-side input filter. */\nexport function classifyInput(raw: string): InputVerdict {\n  const t = normalize(raw);\n  if (!t) return { kind: \"empty\" };\n  if (containsWord(t, WELLBEING)) return { kind: \"wellbeing\" };\n  if (containsWord(t, PROFANITY) || containsWord(t, ADULT_TOPICS)) return { kind: \"unsafe\" };\n  if (INJECTION_PATTERNS.some((re) => re.test(t))) return { kind: \"injection\" };\n  return { kind: \"ok\", answerRequest: ANSWER_REQUEST_PATTERNS.some((re) => re.test(t)) };\n}\n\n/* ---------------------------- Solution leakage ----------------------------- */\n\nconst esc = (s: string) => s.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, \"\\\\$&\");\n\nfunction actionLabel(palette: Palette, action: string) {\n  const label = palette.actions.find((a) => a.action === action)?.label ?? action;\n  return normalize(label).replace(/^ke\\s+/, \"\");\n}\nfunction condLabel(palette: Palette, cond: string) {\n  return normalize(palette.conditions?.find((c) => c.id === cond)?.label ?? cond);\n}\n\ntype Token = { re: string; weight: number };\n\nfunction tokensFor(blocks: Block[], palette: Palette): Token[] {\n  const out: Token[] = [];\n  let i = 0;\n  while (i < blocks.length) {\n    const b = blocks[i];\n    if (b.kind === \"action\") {\n      let count = 1;\n      while (\n        i + count < blocks.length &&\n        blocks[i + count].kind === \"action\" &&\n        (blocks[i + count] as typeof b).action === b.action\n      ) {\n        count++;\n      }\n      const l = esc(actionLabel(palette, b.action));\n      const re =\n        count === 1\n          ? l\n          : `(?:${l}(?:[\\\\s\\\\S]{0,40}?${l}){${count - 1}}|${l}\\\\W{0,12}(?:sebanyak\\\\s*)?${count}\\\\s*(?:x|kali))`;\n      out.push({ re, weight: count });\n      i += count;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (b.kind === \"repeat\") {\n      out.push({ re: `(?:ulangi|ulang|diulang)\\\\W{0,12}(?:sebanyak\\\\s*)?${b.times}`, weight: 1 });\n      out.push(...tokensFor(b.body, palette));\n    } else {\n      out.push({ re: `(?:jika|kalau|if)\\\\W{0,12}${esc(condLabel(palette, b.cond))}`, weight: 1 });\n      out.push(...tokensFor(b.then, palette));\n      if (b.else.length) {\n        out.push({ re: \"(?:lainnya|kalau tidak|jika tidak|else)\", weight: 0 });\n        out.push(...tokensFor(b.else, palette));\n      }\n    }\n    i++;\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\n/**\n * FR-AI-03: detect whether a text spells out the complete solution\n * (all solution blocks, in order). Partial hints are allowed.\n */\nexport function leaksSolution(text: string, mission: Pick<Mission, \"solution\" | \"palette\">): boolean {\n  const tokens = tokensFor(mission.solution, mission.palette);\n  const weight = tokens.reduce((a, t) => a + t.weight, 0);\n  if (weight < 2) return false;\n  const pattern = new RegExp(tokens.map((t) => t.re).join(\"[\\\\s\\\\S]{0,120}?\"));\n  return pattern.test(normalize(text));\n}\n\n/** FR-AI-S2: output filter applied to every sentence before it reaches the child. */\nexport function checkOutput(\n  text: string,\n  mission: Pick<Mission, \"solution\" | \"palette\">,\n): { ok: true; text: string } | { ok: false; reason: \"unsafe\" | \"leak\" } {\n  const t = normalize(text);\n  if (containsWord(t, PROFANITY) || containsWord(t, ADULT_TOPICS)) return { ok: false, reason: \"unsafe\" };\n  if (leaksSolution(text, mission)) return { ok: false, reason: \"leak\" };\n  return { ok: true, text: maskPII(text).text };\n}\n\n/** Split streamed text into complete sentences, returning the unfinished rest. */\nexport function splitSentences(buffer: string): { sentences: string[]; rest: string } {\n  const sentences: string[] = [];\n  const re = /[^.!?\\n]*[.!?\\n]+(?:\\s*\\p{Extended_Pictographic}[\\uFE0F\\u200D\\p{Extended_Pictographic}]*)*\\s*/gu;\n  let last = 0;\n  let m: RegExpExecArray | null;\n  while ((m = re.exec(buffer))) {\n    if (m[0].length === 0) {\n      re.lastIndex++;\n      continue;\n    }\n    sentences.push(m[0]);\n    last = m.index + m[0].length;\n  }\n  return { sentences, rest: buffer.slice(last) };\n}\n","Description":"Bibi AI guardrails: PII masking, injection/unsafe detection, solution-leak detection, output filtering.","Overwrite":false,"TargetFile":"e:\\codekids\\src\\lib\\bibi\\guardrails.ts","toolAction":"Writing Bibi guardrails","toolSummary":"Bibi guardrails"}}]}
